# Packaging and privacy

## Artifacts

- Build in clean `dist/` — wheel contains runtime modules, TCSS, bundled resources, metadata, license only
- Wheel must not contain: tests, caches, logs, history, wordlist, config, journal, snapshots
- Verify version consistency in `pyproject.toml`, `spell-sync version`, wheel METADATA, sdist PKG-INFO

## Source export

- Use `git archive` from the public repository root
- Never zip or archive a parent workspace containing private repos or personal data

## Diagnostics privacy

- Technical log and support report exports must pass redaction tests before release
- Do not embed raw event payloads with user dictionary content in shipped artifacts

## Publication

- No push/tag/publish without explicit owner request: see `project-safety` rule.
- Pre-publication: run `privacy-export` skill checklist and full CI

Manual testing reference: `@docs/MANUAL_TESTING.md`
